From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:03:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Add focus statistics

Add a contrast figure for a contrast detection autofocus to the software
ISP statistics: the squared difference between neighbouring pairs of
green pixels of one Bayer site, horizontally and vertically, summed over
the central half of the image, together with the sum of the green
values so that the contrast can be taken relative to the brightness.
The pairs make it a band-pass around a period of eight pixels, which
still responds away from the focus and stays above the pixel noise.

The figure is gathered from the mapped input frame on the frames that
have statistics, for unpacked 8, 10 and 12 bit Bayer formats. Other
formats report no samples.
